\nNote that we had to flip the sign of the inequality since we divided by a negative number.\n\nHere, the square root is greater than a negative number $(-2),$ so any number we can substitute into the square root will satisfy the inequality. So, the solution is the domain of the square root.\n\nTo find the domain, we recall that the expression under the square root must be greater than or equal to $0:$\n\n$$\nx+3\\ge 0\\,⇒\\,x\\ge -3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\ge -3.$" 13194139534590 true] [17592186297524 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297525 13194139534590 true] [17592186297524 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297526 13194139534590 true] [17592186297524 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297527 13194139534590 true] [17592186297524 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297528 13194139534590 true] [17592186297524 1000 #edb/ref 17592186297529 13194139534590 true] [17592186297524 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534590 true] [17592186297524 1041 "selection" 13194139534590 true] [17592186297524 1104 #edb/ref 17592186297527 13194139534590 true] [17592186297524 1110 #uuid "39ba0ef3-55c2-596e-9077-5c3996b511e7" 13194139534590 true] [17592186297525 1034 "x\\ge -7" 13194139534590 true] [17592186297525 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534590 true] [17592186297525 1111 #uuid "0f24499e-1383-57cf-8eae-e6fa2bb83692" 13194139534590 true] [17592186297526 1034 "x\\le -3" 13194139534590 true] [17592186297526 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534590 true] [17592186297526 1111 #uuid "a1b98672-3647-5ead-b442-45ec7ffa1a5d" 13194139534590 true] [17592186297527 1034 "x\\ge -3" 13194139534590 true] [17592186297527 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534590 true] [17592186297527 1111 #uuid "e57c30e1-b45f-5d0b-94da-cefe0c6162e9" 13194139534590 true] [17592186297528 1034 "x\\ge 1" 13194139534590 true] [17592186297528 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534590 true] [17592186297528 1111 #uuid "b36b382f-8d51-53af-83b3-78bd61e8fead" 13194139534590 true] [17592186297529 1034 "x\\le 1" 13194139534590 true] [17592186297529 